A||||8||JetroGT||The Dealer Sucks!||||8||
Z||000000||JetroGT||01-29-2001||04:32 PM||||I called up the dealer today to get a quote for parts and labor to replace all of the ball joints on my 87GT. He says, "we don't even have books that go that far back" and "we don't even have Fiero listed". I went to Allen Young Pontiac in Fort Worth. They suck! The whole time the guy was laughing. When I buy a new car I won't go there.||||reg||8
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-29-2001||04:47 PM||||A lot of dealers are like that.  I went through the same thing when the Fiero was still a relatively new car (1990), so don't feel bad.<P>I suggest writing a letter to the owner/manager of the dealership.  Explain what happened, how you were treated and that you will not give them anymore business.  Also tell them you will recommend to everyone you know to avoid them at all costs.<P>Be polite about it and word it in such a way that you don't come off as a jerk.  Be professional about it......you may receive a reply from him.  I would still not take my car to them, but at least you know you got through to them.<P><BR>If I were closer to you I would install the balljoints.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||01-29-2001||05:35 PM||||I thought one day a gang of Fieros would get together and go to a dealer and ask for oil changes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just to see the look on their faces, and let them know were still here, and looking good.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||10
Z||000003||fiero56||01-29-2001||06:27 PM||||My dealer is great! I know it's a rare find, but I go to one of the local Pontiac dealers, and they are awsome. The parts department is always very fast(unless you go in at lunch time) and friendly. The service is the best I have ever seen, and they are very well priced, I think. I've only had service performed twice. First time was had them align my Formula after I installed poly bushings. Took less than two hours, was $50 and they supplied a printout. They also told me if they took longer than quoted, they would provide transportation to and from work for the day until my car was finished(this for a 20yr old kid with no money for a new car for a long time). They finished with time to spare, I was very impressed.<P>I was just there again on Friday having them remove the McGuard wheel locks from my Formula because I lost the key. Took the service department 25 minutes and only cost me half-hour worth of labor, $30. They also put on new lug nuts and black nylon caps free of charge. The only catch is they want me to continue business <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. They always admire my Fieros and comment on what great cars they are. I'm not BS'ing here, this is the truth.<BR>If you're in the Dayton, OH area, try out Jack Walker Pontiac on Springboro Pike, I've been very impressed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||01-29-2001||06:55 PM||||hey i like the idea of goin to the dealer all at the same time.  hehe.  of course the lube tech would hate fieros forever. hehe.  we should all get together after daytona and get lubed.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||14
Z||000005||trigger||01-29-2001||09:25 PM||||hello,<BR>I try to do as much of the work as I can by myself, if that fails my boss (Mike Deutmeyer at Deutmeyer Auto Advantage in Dyersville) and I work on it.  I get free lift access plus more air tools than I know what to do with.  However if he works on it I get to pay labor.  I took my car to one used car dealership in Dyersville and they did a good alignment for me.  I could tell especially since they put in a new ball joint.  Then another garage was putting in my belt tensioner and they had to get it straight from G.M. and then after they did that they charged me for a gallon of antifreeze.  I think they must have dumped the resevoir and refilled it.  Don't know what that had to do with the belt tensior.  Otherwise I get all my parts and a lot of service from my mechanic.  If you need parts try Mike Weber in Ryan, Iowa.  It's called Weber Interprises used car dealer and service.  He has parts cars.  I'm buying an 87 from him this spring.  Sorry it's so long.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||01-29-2001||09:58 PM||||well 56, now I know who to take my car to when I drive back to that area (I'll be driving my daughters car back once I get it built for her - hope to catch up with you than too!)<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||01-30-2001||12:27 AM||||Trigger,<P>The belt tensioner actually covers up a hole in the block that is the opening for the water pump when the block is used in an S-10, that's why they had to drain some coolant.   ||||reg||
Z||000008||trigger||01-30-2001||09:24 AM||||thanks standard.  I didn't know that.  Oh well my car still isn't going back there.  He left it parked outside with both doors unlocked and the keys in the ignition.  So, I took the radio face, the keys and locked the doors.  Next day I go to give him the keys back and the car was in the shop, they jacked it up and pushed it in.  When my dad had his 54 ford f100 there to get brakes  they said they drove it in with the e-brake.  Well, they had it for 2 months and did nothing, so dad brought it home and I fixed it.  Turns out the e-brake is non functional.  He must have used park.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||11
